ry with the cashflow evidence. Yvette's intention to reduce to 3 days per week is mentioned only in the suitability report, with no corroboration in the fact-find or cashflow files. The adviser note 'Defo 60?' records an unresolved question, not a confirmed objective; the report treating Anthony's retirement at 60 as established fact is therefore unsupported. The IHT legislative change (item 6) falls within the guard for legislative changes affecting everyone and is not client-specific; no discrepancy arises there. The inheritance and renovation split are corroborated by the adviser notes. The State Pension figures of £11,973 are consistent with the cashflow model inputs but are not independently corroborated by a state pension forecast or fact-find record; this is an evidence gap but lower severity than the Yvette retirement age conflict. The vulnerability overlay: no vulnerability characteristics are recorded in the file that materially alter this assessment. The primary finding is the contradiction between the reported foreseeable change (Yvette retiring at Anthony's age 60) and the cashflow evidence (Yvette retiring at age 67), which is material because it underpins the capacity for loss narrative.","citations":[{"passageId":"P15","source":"Cashflow - Market Crash.md","category":"F","quote":"\"Retire\" age 67 in 2037, \"Illness\" age 104 in 2074, and \"Death\" age 104 in 2074","cells":null},{"passageId":"P6","source":"Cashflow - Market Crash.md","category":"F","quote":"\"Retire\" age 67 in 2033, \"Illness\" age 107 in 2073, and \"Death\" age 107 in 2073","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Cashflow - Tony Predeceases in 2040.md","category":"F","quote":"\"Retire\" age 67 in 2033, \"Illness\" age 107 in 2073, and \"Death\" age 107 in 2073","cells":null},{"passageId":"P17","source":"Cashflow - Tony Predeceases in 2040.md","category":"F","quote":"\"Retire\" age 67 in 2037, \"Illness\" age 104 in 2074, and \"Death\" age 70 in 2040","cells":null},{"passageId":"P