red' — goes beyond what P2 explicitly itemises, meaning those specific elements are asserted in the report but not fully corroborated by independent file evidence. This is not a contradiction but an absence of corroboration for specific service components. The ongoing charge applies across all three Aviva Platform products (pension, ISA, GIA), and while P12 confirms 1% on investment funds transacted, no passage explicitly confirms the multi-product scope stated in the report. The guard that a service the client declined is still disclosed does not apply here — there is no suggestion any service was declined. The guard that the client agreement and report may label the same service differently applies: P2's 'review meeting at least once a year' is consistent with the report's annual suitability review, even if labelled differently. Overall, the rate matches, the annual review element is corroborated, but several specific service components listed in the report lack independent documentary support. This is a disclosure shortfall / missing evidence concern at low-to-moderate severity rather than a direct contradiction. No vulnerability indicators in the file appear to affect this specific requirement materially.","citations":[{"passageId":"P12","source":"Client Agreement To Proceed.md","category":"A","quote":"For most investment funds that we transact on your behalf, we charge an ongoing annual review management charge of 1% (subject to a minimum fee of £100), which is automatically taken from the funds invested.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P2","source":"IMPORT_2.md","category":"A","quote":null,"cells":["Ongoing Advice and Review Services","Review meeting at least once a year and recommendations which may include the following as part of thi"]},{"passageId":"P4","source":"Client Agreement To Proceed.md","category":"A","quote":"Should you choose to proceed with our recommendations, we will provide you with our Ongoing advice and review service, as described in the 'Imp